																		Thanks, Attribution, and Other Matters
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2039383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606101076" alt="MrWrong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2039383)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;" >MrWrong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496541790 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jun 2017 02:03</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2841193">
									

<p>Firstly, the quote that inspired this concept:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I can draw out causes of death from the residual information of the dead, store them in existing weapons, and swap out the causes of death. I can strangle you with a sword, drown you with a train, crush you with a blowtorch, and burn you with a handgun. That is a suitable reason to bear the name of Hel, the queen of Niflheimr who rules over the dead. – Hel, <em>A Certain Magical Index</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Despite inspiration, I made up everything other than the super general premises of it.</p>
<p>Next, allow me to express thank you to the many people who've seen this through: DrMagnus, SunnyClockwork, ARD, and many others on the chat.</p>
<p>Image attributions for this article are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Image 1 by User:Røed of Wikimedia Commons (<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NSB_Di._4.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NSB_Di._4.jpg</a>) under CC BY-SA 2.5</li>
<li>Image 2 by Peter van der Sluijs of Wikimedia Commons (<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Little_fish_in_hand.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Little_fish_in_hand.jpg</a>) under CC BY-SA 3.0</li>
</ul>
<p>This article also features: SCP-3456 (The Orcadian Horsemen) by DrBleep</p>
<p>Other things:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The SCP is originally an analogue to a spacesuit for the mer-person in the addendum. She basically altered the SCP to cover the entire train and then offed herself.</p>
<p>As for the nature of the mer-person, she takes influence from both the merrow and selkie.</p>
<p>The red feathers are analogues to guns for the mer-person, and references the myths on merrows.</p>
<p>The map actually denotes manifestation of SCP-3456, which usually appear in places where war and human suffering occurs.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">As for motive behind this madness, the mer-person is affiliated with some group that monitors 3456 and she was mortally wounded by 3456's attack. Unable to report back to her superiors underneath the sea, she chose to deliver her findings to the next best thing - the Foundation. But she did not know where to find them&#8230; so she created a scene to make them show up.</span></p>
<p>EDIT: After some thought, I will not impose the mer-person's motives. She is still monitoring 3456's activities on the surface, and was attacked by one. Her 'sea-suit' ultimately unravelled while she was travelling in a train.</p>
</div>
</div>
